message.content:
Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows how to create a “flip‑card” that rotates around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy the HTML/CSS into your own project and tweak the dimensions, colors, or rotation axis as you wish.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Obracająca się karta</title>
<style>
/* 1️⃣  Wrapper – gives the card a 3‑D context */
.card-wrapper {
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    perspective: 800px;          /* Needed for 3‑D effect */
    margin: 50px auto;           /* Center horizontally */
}

/* 2️⃣  Card itself – holds front & back faces */
.card {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    position: relative;
    transform-style: preserve-3d; /* Keep children in 3‑D space */
    transition: transform 0.6s ease; /* Smooth animation */
}

/* 3️⃣  Front face */
.card .front,
.card .back {
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    backface-visibility: hidden; /* Hide backside when rotated */
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

/* 4️⃣  Styling for front side */
.card .front {
    background: #fff;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: #333;
}

/* 5️⃣  Styling for back side – rotated 180° so it’s hidden initially */
.card .back {
    background: #f8f8f8;
    transform: rotateY(180deg);   /* Start flipped */
    padding: 20px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: #555;
}

/* 6️⃣  Hover effect – flip the whole card */
.card:hover {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front side -->
        <div class="front">
            <p>Front</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Back side -->
        <div class="back">
            <h3>Tytuł</h3>
            <p>To jest zawartość tylnej strony karty. Możesz tu umieścić dowolny tekst, obrazki czy przyciski.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| **1** | `perspective` on `.card-wrapper` | Gives depth to the 3‑D transformation. |
| **2** | `transform-style: preserve-3d` on `.card` | Keeps child elements (front/back) in 3‑D space. |
| **3** | `backface-visibility: hidden` | Hides the backside of each face when it’s turned away from the viewer. |
| **4** | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on `.back` | Positions the back face behind the front at start. |
| **5** | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on `.card:hover` | Rotates the entire card, bringing the back face to the front. |

#### Customization tips

- **Rotation axis** – change `rotateY` to `rotateX` if you want a vertical flip instead of horizontal.
- **Angle** – use `rotateY(90deg)` for a half‑turn or any other degree value.
- **Speed** – adjust `transition: transform 0.6s ease` to make the flip faster/slower.
- **Perspective** – increase/decrease the `perspective` value to control how pronounced the 3‑D effect looks.

That’s all! Drop this into your page and enjoy a smooth, hover‑activated rotating card.
